---
import { prePurchaseSurveyPage } from '../data/pre-purchase-survey';
import ServiceLayout from '../layouts/ServiceLayout.astro';
import { createServiceSchema } from '../utils/seo';

const serviceSchema = createServiceSchema({
  name: 'Pre-Purchase Yacht Survey',
  serviceType: 'Pre-purchase yacht survey and condition inspection',
  pathname: prePurchaseSurveyPage.pathname,
  description: prePurchaseSurveyPage.description,
  areaServed: prePurchaseSurveyPage.areaServed,
});
---

<ServiceLayout
  title={prePurchaseSurveyPage.title}
  description={prePurchaseSurveyPage.description}
  locale="en"
  routeId="prePurchaseSurvey"
  pathname={prePurchaseSurveyPage.pathname}
  heading={prePurchaseSurveyPage.heading}
  eyebrow={prePurchaseSurveyPage.eyebrow}
  summary={prePurchaseSurveyPage.summary}
  heroImage={prePurchaseSurveyPage.heroImage}
  breadcrumbs={prePurchaseSurveyPage.breadcrumbs}
  primaryCta={prePurchaseSurveyPage.primaryCta}
  secondaryCta={prePurchaseSurveyPage.secondaryCta}
  relatedServices={prePurchaseSurveyPage.relatedServices}
  finalCta={prePurchaseSurveyPage.finalCta}
  structuredData={serviceSchema}
>
  <section aria-labelledby="independent-survey-heading">
    <h2 id="independent-survey-heading">
      Independent Pre-Purchase Yacht Survey
    </h2>
    <p>
      Buying a yacht is a significant financial commitment. A professional
      pre-purchase yacht survey provides an independent assessment of the
      vessel’s condition before the buyer completes the purchase.
    </p>
    <p>
      All Yacht Service carries out pre-purchase surveys for sailing yachts,
      motor yachts and catamarans up to 24 metres. The inspection is intended to
      identify visible defects, safety concerns, maintenance requirements and
      areas that may require further specialist investigation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Surveys are carried out by Aleksandrs Tolkacovs, an IIMS-Certified Yacht
      and Small Craft Marine Surveyor and licensed captain, supported by more
      than 20 years of experience in engineering, quality assurance and
      management.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="survey-includes-heading">
    <h2 id="survey-includes-heading">
      What a Pre-Purchase Yacht Survey Includes
    </h2>
    <p>
      The exact scope depends on the vessel, its construction, equipment,
      location and accessibility. A typical pre-purchase survey may include:
    </p>
    <div class="inspection-grid">
      {
        prePurchaseSurveyPage.inspectionItems.map((item) => (
          <article>
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.description}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="service-note">
      The survey is a non-destructive inspection and is limited to areas and
      equipment that are safely accessible at the time of the survey. Where
      specialist mechanical, electrical, rigging or laboratory investigation is
      recommended, this will be identified in the report.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="survey-importance-heading">
    <h2 id="survey-importance-heading">
      Why a Professional Yacht Survey Is Important Before Buying
    </h2>
    <p>
      Many serious yacht defects are not obvious during a casual viewing. A
      yacht may appear well maintained while still containing structural,
      mechanical, electrical or safety-related problems that could lead to
      substantial repair costs.
    </p>
    <p>
      An independent survey helps the buyer understand the vessel’s actual
      condition, prioritise necessary work and make a better-informed decision
      before completing the purchase.
    </p>
    <p>The report may also support:</p>
    <ul class="service-check-list">
      {prePurchaseSurveyPage.reportUses.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="common-defects-heading">
    <h2 id="common-defects-heading">
      Common Defects Identified During Yacht Surveys
    </h2>
    <p>
      Even apparently well-maintained yachts may contain defects or undocumented
      work. Common findings can include:
    </p>
    <ul class="defect-grid">
      {prePurchaseSurveyPage.commonDefects.map((defect) => <li>{defect}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="survey-process-heading">
    <h2 id="survey-process-heading">
      How the Pre-Purchase Survey Process Works
    </h2>
    <ol class="process-list">
      {
        prePurchaseSurveyPage.processSteps.map((step, index) => (
          <li>
            <div>
              <span aria-hidden="true">
                {String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
              </span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>{step.title}</h3>
              <p>{step.description}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="haul-out-heading">
    <h2 id="haul-out-heading">Haul-Out and Sea Trial</h2>
    <p>
      A comprehensive pre-purchase survey is normally most effective when the
      yacht can be inspected both afloat and out of the water.
    </p>
    <p>
      Haul-out allows inspection of the underwater hull, keel, rudder,
      propellers, shafts, saildrives and underwater fittings.
    </p>
    <p>
      A sea trial provides an opportunity to assess propulsion, steering,
      instrumentation and selected onboard systems under realistic operating
      conditions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Haul-out, marina, fuel and vessel-operating costs are normally arranged
      separately and are not automatically included in the survey fee unless
      specifically stated in the quotation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="survey-report-heading">
    <h2 id="survey-report-heading">
      Clear Survey Report and Practical Recommendations
    </h2>
    <p>
      The survey report explains the vessel’s observed condition in clear and
      practical language. Findings are supported by photographs and prioritised
      so the buyer can distinguish between significant safety concerns,
      important maintenance items and less urgent observations.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reports are normally issued within 48 hours after completion of the
      inspection, subject to the vessel, survey scope and any additional
      information required.
    </p>
    <p>
      The report is prepared for the commissioning client and should not be
      presented as a guarantee of future condition or freedom from defects.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="pre-offer-heading">
    <h2 id="pre-offer-heading">Walkthrough and Pre-Offer Inspection</h2>
    <p>
      For buyers who are not yet ready to commission a full survey, All Yacht
      Service can provide a shorter walkthrough or pre-offer inspection.
    </p>
    <p>
      This service is intended to identify obvious concerns and major warning
      signs before the buyer submits an offer or arranges a comprehensive
      survey.
    </p>
    <p>Depending on the agreed scope, it may include:</p>
    <ul class="service-check-list">
      {prePurchaseSurveyPage.preOfferItems.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p class="service-note">
      A walkthrough or pre-offer inspection is limited in scope and does not
      replace a full pre-purchase yacht survey.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="survey-coverage-heading">
    <h2 id="survey-coverage-heading">
      Pre-Purchase Yacht Surveys Across Spain and the Mediterranean
    </h2>
    <p>
      Based at Marina Greenwich in Altea, All Yacht Service carries out
      pre-purchase yacht surveys throughout Alicante, Costa Blanca, Valencia,
      Barcelona, the Spanish Mediterranean coast and other locations across
      mainland Spain.
    </p>
    <p>
      Surveys in the Balearic Islands, France, Italy, Greece and other European
      or international locations can also be arranged according to the vessel’s
      location, access requirements and survey scope.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="combined-delivery-heading">
    <h2 id="combined-delivery-heading">
      Combining a Survey with Yacht Delivery
    </h2>
    <p>
      When the purchase is completed, All Yacht Service can also arrange
      {' '}<a class="text-link" href="/yacht-delivery"
        >professional yacht delivery</a
      >{' '}
      to the vessel’s new marina or destination.
    </p>
    <p>
      Combining the survey and delivery services provides continuity from the
      technical inspection through to passage preparation, arrival and handover.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="why-survey-heading">
    <h2 id="why-survey-heading">Why Choose All Yacht Service?</h2>
    <ul class="service-check-list">
      {prePurchaseSurveyPage.whyChoose.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>
</ServiceLayout>
